<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  OnePlus 8 Pro (instantnoodlep) repowerd device config, Ubuntu Touch port.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  repowerd reports auto-brightness availability to Lomiri System Settings via
  com.lomiri.Repowerd.getBrightnessParams(); the last field of that struct is
  what gates the "Adjust automatically" checkbox
  (qml-plugins/brightness/PageComponent.qml: visible: autoBrightnessAvailable).
  Stock Ubuntu Touch ships only config-default.xml, which hardcodes
  config_automatic_brightness_available=false and leaves both auto-brightness
  arrays EMPTY, so the checkbox is hidden on every device without an override.
  There was no instantnoodlep override, so the toggle never appeared.

  The hardware is fine: OnePlus's own Android overlay
  (device/oneplus/instantnoodlep/overlay/OPlusFrameworksResTarget/res/values/
  config.xml) sets config_automatic_brightness_available=true, and sensorfw
  exposes a working /SensorManager/alssensor reading about 296 lux indoors
  (verified live 2026-09-02, after the persist-partition fix revived the SLPI).

  WHERE THE CURVE COMES FROM
  config_autoBrightnessLevels is copied verbatim from that OnePlus overlay.
  OnePlus expresses the response curve in NITS (config_autoBrightnessDisplay-
  ValuesNits), which Android 11+ prefers but repowerd does not understand.
  repowerd reads only config_autoBrightnessLcdBacklightValues, on a 0 to 255
  scale. So each nits value was converted to a backlight value by linear
  interpolation through the device's own measured nits to backlight table (the
  65 entry config_screenBrightnessNits / config_screenBrightnessBacklight pair
  in the same overlay). That keeps the factory response curve rather than
  inventing one.

  One deliberate deviation: the darkest point interpolates to 3/255, below
  repowerd's own config_screenBrightnessSettingMinimum of 10. It is clamped to
  10 so a pitch dark room cannot drive the panel to near black.

  HOW IT IS LOADED
  The rootfs is a read only loop image, so /usr/share/powerd/device_configs
  cannot be edited. repowerd honours $REPOWERD_DEVICE_CONFIG_DIR, so this file
  is installed to /usr/lib/halium/repowerd-device-configs/ and pointed at by
  /etc/systemd/system/repowerd.service.d/autobrightness.conf.

  Note the unit also has EnvironmentFile=-/etc/default/repowerd, which looks
  like the natural hook, but /etc/default is NOT in
  /etc/system-image/writable-paths and is read only on this image. Of the
  candidates only /etc/systemd/system and /userdata are writable, hence the
  drop in plus /userdata split.

  repowerd always parses config-default.xml from that directory, which is why
  this file keeps that name instead of config-instantnoodlep.xml (repowerd's
  device name detection was not relied upon).

  To revert: rm /etc/systemd/system/repowerd.service.d/autobrightness.conf,
  systemctl daemon-reload, systemctl restart repowerd. Everything else in this
  file matches the stock defaults.
-->
